         "text": [
            {
                "text": "#### Relating shapes\n\nSince our body was initially used to perform counting, the next step for us to be able to count would be to create shapes that, when we look at them, remind us of our hands and, thus, we could do the counting.\n\nIn this lesson, we will see how some peoples used shapes that resemble the human body to count.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f7b09a23-2fd5-457a-9f62-6126191720ac",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f7b09a23-2fd5-457a-9f62-6126191720ac",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "9618a83e-f232-49db-84f6-fc3455a3f1d1",
                "text": "Original text",
                "page": "index.html?page=class_content&arg=687ee328-19bb-4a65-ab46-7d707a2e11dc",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2024",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
                "text": "#### Circles\n\nThe first step to make some connection with our body is to look at it and identify a shape that reminds us of something.\n\nFor example, if you dipped your fingertips in ink and then pressed them onto paper, you would get something like circles.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.circle {width: 100px; height: 100px; background-color: #82d6f5; border-radius: 50%; }</style><div class=\"circle\"></div> <div class=\"circle\"></div> <div class=\"circle\"></div> <div class=\"circle\"></div>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "461b6e4d-de5f-41a0-9e6a-1231ba552d4b",
